{%- comment -%}
  Search Console verification + GA4.

  The theme shipped with no analytics of any kind: no GA4, no GTM, no Search Console
  verification. That is the reason nobody can say which SEO change moved which number,
  and why there is no baseline to measure this sprint against. Shopify's own reporting
  does not cover search impressions, queries or the Google Business Profile, so it is
  not a substitute.

  Both values are optional and live in Theme settings > Kilowash storefront. Nothing is
  emitted until they are filled in, so this snippet is inert on a store that has not
  connected the accounts yet.

  Deliberately not gated on request.design_mode: Search Console needs to read the
  verification tag on the live storefront, and GA4 sessions from the theme editor are a
  rounding error next to the cost of forgetting why no data arrived.

  Rendered from layout/theme.liquid <head>.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if settings.kw_gsc_verification != blank -%}
  <meta name="google-site-verification" content="{{ settings.kw_gsc_verification | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- if settings.kw_ga4_id != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    RemoteAsset is disabled deliberately for this one line. gtag.js must be fetched
    from Google's own domain to function, so it cannot be served from the Shopify CDN;
    the check is correct in general and simply does not apply here.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% # theme-check-disable RemoteAsset %}
  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={{ settings.kw_ga4_id | escape }}"></script>
  {% # theme-check-enable RemoteAsset %}
  <script>
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag() {
      dataLayer.push(arguments);
    }
    gtag('js', new Date());
    gtag('config', {{ settings.kw_ga4_id | json }});
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
